title: `py.test.xfail()` imported through `from py.test import xfail` marks the test as an expected failure
origin: issue #310 P3, in an import spelling. With py 1.11.0 installed, pytest 9.1.1 reports `py.test.xfail()` as `1 xfailed`. v0.6.0 passes this with zero findings
=== head: app/__init__.py ===

=== head: app/billing.py ===
def total(items):
    return round(sum(items), 2)
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
from py.test import xfail

from app.billing import total


def test_total():
    assert total([50.0, 28.75]) == 78.75
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
from py.test import xfail

from app.billing import total


def test_total():
    xfail("later")
    assert total([50.0, 28.75]) == 78.75
